The attached image (Figure 4) illustrates the active transport of Nano-11 nanoparticles to draining lymph nodes by antigen-presenting cells (APCs). Panel A shows flow cytometry plots at days 1, 2, and 7 post-immunization, identifying Nano-11-containing myeloid cells, particularly migratory dendritic cells (MigDCs). Panel B highlights that the peak percentage of Nano-11-containing myeloid cells in the lymph node occurs on day 2. Panel C further reveals that MigDCs comprise the majority (60-80%) of Nano-11-positive cells. Panel D demonstrates significantly higher mean fluorescence intensity (MFI) in MigDCs, indicating greater Nano-11 uptake per cell compared to other APC subtypes, supporting efficient delivery and targeting to these immunopotentiating cells.